      "es their mouse left/right across the viewport, the video scrubs forward/backward",
      " through its timeline. Implementation details:\n\n- The video is paused on load at",
      " `currentTime = 0`.\n- Track the mouse's horizontal position as a normalized valu",
      "e (0 to 1) across `window.innerWidth`.\n- On each `mousemove`, compute the delta ",
      "from the previous X position. Multiply that delta by a `SENSITIVITY` constant of",
      " `0.8` and by the video's `duration` to get a time offset.\n- Maintain a `targetT",
      "ime` that accumulates these offsets, clamped between 0 and `duration`.\n- Use the",
      " video's `seeked` event to chain seeks: when a seek completes, if `targetTime` h",
      "as diverged from `currentTime` by more than 0.01s, seek again. This prevents dro",
      "pped seeks since the browser can only process one seek at a time.\n- Use a `useRe",
      "f` to store mutable state (`targetTime`, `isSeeking` flag, `prevX`) to avoid re-",
      "renders.\n- The `<video>` element has attributes: `muted`, `playsInline`, `preloa",
